findings.claim:
AWS running costs in London:
- gp3 disk $0.0928/GB-month, charged while stopped;
- snapshots $0.053/GB-month, or $0.01325 archived;
- internet egress $0.09/GB for the first 10 TB 'beyond the global free tier' (memory: 100 GB/month);
- public IPv4 $0.005/h.
DCV itself has 'no additional charge' on EC2. New accounts start with a 0 vCPU quota for 'Running On-Demand G and VT instances', so a quota request comes first.
